item.content:encoded:
&lt;h1&gt;


Opportunity Discovery: When "Find a Problem" Isn't Working
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The Problem in Concrete Terms
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You've read the advice: "Talk to customers," "Scratch your own itch," "Look for complaints on Reddit." You've done the interviews. You've scanned the forums. You've listed fifty problems. And you're still stuck—either because every problem feels too small, too crowded, too hard to monetize, or because you can't tell which ones are &lt;em&gt;real&lt;/em&gt; versus just loud.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The stuckness usually looks like one of three things:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The "So What?" Problem&lt;/strong&gt;: You found a genuine pain point, but the people who have it won't pay to solve it. They workaround. They complain. They don't buy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The "Already Solved" Problem&lt;/strong&gt;: Every problem you find has three funded competitors and a graveyard of failed attempts. You can't articulate why &lt;em&gt;you&lt;/em&gt; would win.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The "Vague Hunch" Problem&lt;/strong&gt;: You sense an opportunity in a space you know (your industry, your hobby, your workflow), but you can't sharpen it into a specific, testable hypothesis. You're paralyzed by the gap between "this feels broken" and "here's a product people will pay for."&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The common thread: you're treating opportunity discovery as &lt;em&gt;research&lt;/em&gt; when it's actually &lt;em&gt;hypothesis generation under uncertainty&lt;/em&gt;. Research gathers facts. Hypothesis generation makes bets. You're stuck because you're trying to research your way to certainty before placing a bet—and that certainty doesn't exist.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Why the Usual Fixes Fail
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer interviews&lt;/strong&gt; fail when you ask "What problems do you have?" People invent problems they think you want to hear, or they describe symptoms without root causes. They can't tell you what they'd pay for because they don't know what's possible.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scratch-your-own-itch&lt;/strong&gt; fails when your itch is too niche, too idiosyncratic, or already solved by a tool you haven't found yet. It also fails when you're the &lt;em&gt;only&lt;/em&gt; one with that itch.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Forum/complaint mining&lt;/strong&gt; fails because complaints are noise. People complain about things they'll never pay to fix. They complain about pricing, about missing features that only they want, about bugs in free tools. The signal-to-noise ratio is terrible without a filter.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market sizing spreadsheets&lt;/strong&gt; fail because TAM/SAM/SOM for a &lt;em&gt;new&lt;/em&gt; opportunity is fiction. You're multiplying guesses by assumptions. The precision creates false confidence.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competitor analysis&lt;/strong&gt; fails when you study what exists instead of what's missing. You end up building a "better" version of a product nobody wants, or you talk yourself out of a space because "it's crowded" without understanding &lt;em&gt;why&lt;/em&gt; the incumbents are vulnerable.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;All these methods share a flaw: they assume the opportunity is &lt;em&gt;out there&lt;/em&gt; waiting to be discovered. It's not. An opportunity is a &lt;em&gt;match&lt;/em&gt; between a specific problem, a specific audience, a specific solution approach, and a specific go-to-market motion. You don't find it. You construct it—and then you test whether the construction holds.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Step-by-Step Solution: From Vague Space to Testable Hypothesis
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Step 1: Pick a Hunting Ground You Can Actually Reach
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Stop hunting "everywhere." Pick &lt;em&gt;one&lt;/em&gt; domain where you have either:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Access&lt;/strong&gt;: You can reach decision-makers this week without cold outreach (former colleagues, communities you're in, industries you've worked in)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Insight&lt;/strong&gt;: You understand the workflow, constraints, and language better than 90% of outsiders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Write down the domain. Be specific: not "healthcare" but "outpatient physical therapy clinics with 3-10 providers." Not "e-commerce" but "Shopify merchants doing $100K-$2M/year who manage their own fulfillment."&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you have multiple domains, rank them by (access × insight) and pick the top one. You can run this process in parallel later. For now, one.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Step 2: Map the Workflow, Not the Problems
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Get access to 3-5 people in that domain. Don't interview them about problems. &lt;strong&gt;Watch them work.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ask: "Can I screen-share for 30 minutes while you do [core task: scheduling, quoting, reporting, onboarding, inventory reconciliation]?" Take timestamped notes on:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Every tool they switch between&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Every copy-paste, export-import, manual calculation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Every "I have to remember to..." or "I always forget to..."&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Every spreadsheet that shadows a SaaS tool&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Every time they ask a colleague "Hey, did you...?"&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Every complaint about their current stack—&lt;em&gt;especially&lt;/em&gt; the ones they've stopped complaining about because "that's just how it is"&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You're not looking for problems. You're looking for &lt;strong&gt;friction that has become invisible to them&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Do this with 3-5 people. Pattern-match across the sessions. The opportunities live in the overlaps.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Step 3: Extract Candidate Opportunities Using the "Three Filters"
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For each friction pattern you observed, write a one-sentence candidate in this format:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[Specific role] spends [time/frequency] doing [manual workaround] because [root constraint], and they'd pay [proxy for value] to eliminate it.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Example: &lt;em&gt;"Clinic office managers spend 4-6 hours/week manually reconciling insurance payments against bank deposits because their EHR doesn't auto-match remittance codes, and they'd pay $200-400/mo to eliminate it."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Now apply three filters. Kill any candidate that fails any filter.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Filter 1: Budget Authority Access&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Can the person feeling the pain &lt;em&gt;also&lt;/em&gt; sign the check? Or is there a clear, short path to the buyer? If the office manager feels the pain but the clinic owner decides—and you can't reach clinic owners—kill it. You don't have a distribution path.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Filter 2: Workaround Cost &amp;gt; Switching Cost&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Quantify the current workaround in hours × hourly rate (or revenue loss). Compare to your estimated implementation effort for them. If the workaround costs $500/mo in time and your tool takes 20 hours to onboard, that's a 4-month payback. Acceptable. If payback is 18 months, kill it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Filter 3: No Strategic Incumbent Lock-in&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Is the friction caused by a missing feature in their core system (EHR, ERP, POS)? If yes, the incumbent &lt;em&gt;will&lt;/em&gt; build it—or already has it on the roadmap. You're a feature, not a product. Kill it unless you have a structural reason they won't/can't (regulatory, architectural, business model conflict).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You should have 3-8 candidates surviving. If zero, go back to Step 2 with a different hunting ground.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Step 4: Sharpen Each Survivor into a Testable Hypothesis
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For each surviving candidate, write a &lt;strong&gt;hypothesis card&lt;/strong&gt; with these fields:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Field&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Example&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Target&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Office managers at 3-10 provider PT clinics&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pain&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Manual insurance payment reconciliation (4-6 hrs/wk)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Current Workaround&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Export CSVs from EHR + bank, VLOOKUP in Excel, flag mismatches&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Now&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Payers shifting to ERA/835 but EHRs lag on auto-posting; clinics adding providers faster than admin headcount&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solution Concept&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Browser extension that reads bank + EHR exports, auto-matches, surfaces exceptions&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Value Proxy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;$300/mo = 10 hrs saved @ $30/hr loaded cost&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Go-to-Market&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Direct to office managers via PT billing Facebook groups + state association newsletters&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Riskiest Assumption&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Office managers can install a browser extension without IT approval&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Test&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Build a Google Sheet + Apps Script prototype; get 3 offices to use it for 2 weeks; measure time saved&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Riskiest Assumption&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Test&lt;/strong&gt; fields are the only ones that matter. Everything else is context. If you can't name a specific, cheap test that would falsify your riskiest assumption in 2 weeks, the hypothesis isn't sharp enough. Sharpen or kill.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Step 5: Run the Cheapest Test That Could Fail
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Do not build an MVP. Do not design a landing page. Do not set up ads.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Run the test from your hypothesis card. The test must:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cost &amp;lt; $100 and &amp;lt; 20 hours of your time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce a clear &lt;strong&gt;pass/fail signal&lt;/strong&gt; on the riskiest assumption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Involve &lt;em&gt;real people from your target&lt;/em&gt; doing &lt;em&gt;real work&lt;/em&gt; (or a realistic simulation)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Examples of valid tests:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Concierge&lt;/strong&gt;: You manually do the task for 3 users using their actual data; measure time/errors vs. their current process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Wizard of Oz&lt;/strong&gt;: Build a form that looks automated;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://smtm-store.pages.dev/exp-1794772797/?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=article&amp;amp;utm_campaign=exp-1794772797" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Start here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I built a welding positioner (a motorized rotator for pipe and round work) and wrote its controller: an ESP32-P4 touchscreen board, LVGL 9.6, a NEMA 23 stepper and a PUL/DIR driver.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A TIG welder with high-frequency (HF) start throws a lot of RF noise. It can glitch an I2C touch controller right next to a motor that is turning a workpiece. These are six decisions in the firmware that came from that problem. Each one was checked against the code of release v2.4.1.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The cover image is a banner with an LVGL simulator capture of the main screen. It is not a photo of my machine.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fbecpd0ddo69elh3flkwv.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fbecpd0ddo69elh3flkwv.png" alt="Main screen of the controller" width="800" height="480"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;The Continuous screen. This is an LVGL simulator capture at 800 x 480, not a photo of the screen.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


1. STOP acts on touch-down
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A normal LVGL button fires on click, which means on release. With HF noise, the release may never arrive as a clean event. So every button labelled Stop also listens for the press itself. This is in &lt;code&gt;src/ui/screens.cpp&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight cpp"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;lv_obj_add_event_cb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;btn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;cb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;LV_EVENT_CLICKED&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;user_data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// STOP also fires on touch-down: a held press that is lost to touch read errors (HF) must still stop.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;strcmp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;UI_LABEL_STOP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;lv_obj_add_event_cb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;btn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;cb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;LV_EVENT_PRESSED&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;user_data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This came in v2.4.1. The release notes give a second reason: the lift can no longer land on a START button that replaced STOP.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


2. A touch read error is not a release
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The GT911 touch controller sits on I2C. A failed read during HF is a missing sample. It does not tell you the finger lifted. If the read callback reports RELEASED, LVGL fires a click on the held button, and the next good read can press whatever now sits under the finger.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The callback in &lt;code&gt;src/ui/lvgl_hal.cpp&lt;/code&gt; keeps the press for a short time after the last good read. The rule is in &lt;code&gt;src/ui/test_hal_logic.h&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight cpp"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;static&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;constexpr&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;uint32_t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;TOUCH_FAIL_HOLD_MS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;150u&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;inline&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;bool&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;touch_hold_press_on_failed_read&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;bool&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;lastPressed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;uint32_t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;nowMs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;uint32_t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;lastGoodMs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;lastPressed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;uint32_t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;nowMs&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;lastGoodMs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;TOUCH_FAIL_HOLD_MS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;After 150 ms the press is cancelled with &lt;code&gt;lv_indev_wait_release()&lt;/code&gt;. The jog stops and no click fires. A flag then blocks new presses until a good read shows no finger. Without it, a finger still on the glass could become a new press on the button that replaced the old one.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


3. Fault reset never starts rotation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In &lt;code&gt;src/control/control.cpp&lt;/code&gt;, a successful reset ends with a transition of the state machine to IDLE. Rotation needs a new start command after that.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The reset has a race to handle too. A fault can latch while the reset is being processed. &lt;code&gt;safety_check_ui_reset()&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;src/safety/safety.cpp&lt;/code&gt; reads a fault generation counter first and checks it again before and after clearing. If the counter moved, the reset returns false and the new fault stays latched. That fix is also from v2.4.1.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


4. Heartbeats, and a clock race
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The safety task watches the other tasks. It latches a fault when the control loop stops publishing, when the input task heartbeat goes stale, or when the LVGL loop stalls for 2 seconds. It also latches HMI STALE when the touch controller fails 100 reads in a row. When one of these latches during motion, the machine goes to the E-STOP state and stops. This stop acts through firmware and the driver ENA input. It does not cut motor power, and I have not measured the stop time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The subtle part is the clock. Another task can write its timestamp between the moment the checker reads &lt;code&gt;millis()&lt;/code&gt; and the moment it loads the stamp. The stamp is then a few milliseconds ahead of &lt;code&gt;now&lt;/code&gt;, and unsigned subtraction reads that as about 49 days old. A healthy task looks dead. v2.4.0 fixed this in &lt;code&gt;src/control/input_policy.h&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight cpp"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;inline&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;bool&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;timestamp_within&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;uint32_t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;uint32_t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;stamp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;uint32_t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;deadline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;int32_t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;age&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;static_cast&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;int32_t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;stamp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;age&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;age&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;static_cast&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;int32_t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;deadline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The changelog says this rare race could stop a weld with HMI STALE or PEDAL INPUT, or drop a held jog.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


5. Flash writes only at rest
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Saving settings to flash stalls both cores and can delay the E-STOP interrupt. So &lt;code&gt;storage_flush()&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;src/storage/storage.cpp&lt;/code&gt; writes only in IDLE or ESTOP:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight cpp"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;auto&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;atRest&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;SystemState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;control_get_state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;STATE_IDLE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;STATE_ESTOP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;It checks twice, with a 10 ms wait in between to let a start that is already being dispatched become visible. The safety task also skips its heartbeat checks while a flash write is in progress.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


6. The same UI runs on a PC
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The simulator's CMake file compiles the firmware's own &lt;code&gt;src/ui/screens/*.cpp&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;screens.cpp&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;theme.cpp&lt;/code&gt; into a Windows SDL program. I use it to review screens, run UI self-tests and dump screenshots before flashing. The control, speed, storage and safety logic is covered by native tests that use fake clocks and a fake driver. The README states 480 native tests, and CI also runs the simulator self-tests and a layout audit.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fo9096040pazp5uc4kbg7.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fo9096040pazp5uc4kbg7.png" alt="Fault screen with reset blocked" width="800" height="480"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;The fault screen while E-STOP is pressed. Simulator capture.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What it does not do
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;E-STOP is not a safety relay. It acts through GPIO34, firmware and the driver ENA input. It does not cut motor power. An open E-STOP wire can read as healthy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stop time is not measured. Calibration accuracy is not measured either.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The machine has one axis and no encoder. RPM and progress are calculated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Simulator screenshots show the UI only. They say nothing about touch under HF.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The release notes list known limits, for example that Pulse programs have no direction control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;I flashed v2.4.1 on my machine on 2026-11-15 and tested it: motion, pedal, E-STOP and TIG HF start work. That is one machine.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This post was written by an AI agent (Claude Code) from the project repo, and every fact in it was checked against the code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Links
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Source and docs: &lt;a href="https://github.com/catorendal-a11y/DIY-Welding-Positioner-ESP32-P4" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/catorendal-a11y/DIY-Welding-Positioner-ESP32-P4&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Release v2.4.1, with a Windows simulator: &lt;a href="https://github.com/catorendal-a11y/DIY-Welding-Positioner-ESP32-P4/releases/tag/v2.4.1" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/catorendal-a11y/DIY-Welding-Positioner-ESP32-P4/releases/tag/v2.4.1&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demo video (real hardware, earlier UI): &lt;a href="https://youtu.be/GygLl6XY-TM" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://youtu.be/GygLl6XY-TM&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Question: have you built touch input near an HF arc, and would you hold a press for 150 ms after a failed read like this?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;NVIDIA, CVS Health, Wells Fargo, Northrop Grumman and thousands of other large employers post their jobs on Workday. You know these sites by the address: &lt;code&gt;something.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/SomeCareerSite&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The page itself is a JavaScript app, so fetching its HTML gives you almost nothing. But the app loads every job from a small JSON API, and that API is public: no login, no key, no cookies. It is the same request your browser makes when you open the site. This post shows how to use it, and the four gotchas that will silently cost you jobs if you do not know about them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


1. Read the three parts from the URL
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Open the company's careers page, click any job, and look at the address:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;https://nvidia.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/NVIDIAExternalCareerSite/job/US-CA-Santa-Clara/...
^^^^^^ ^^^                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
tenant data center                 site
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;tenant&lt;/strong&gt;: the company's code, &lt;code&gt;nvidia&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;data center&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;wd1&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;wd3&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;wd5&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;wd12&lt;/code&gt; and so on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;site&lt;/strong&gt;: the career site name, &lt;code&gt;NVIDIAExternalCareerSite&lt;/code&gt;. Skip the language part (&lt;code&gt;en-US&lt;/code&gt;) if there is one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You cannot guess these from the company name. NVIDIA is &lt;code&gt;nvidia.wd5/NVIDIAExternalCareerSite&lt;/code&gt;, Northrop Grumman is &lt;code&gt;ngc.wd1/Northrop_Grumman_External_Site&lt;/code&gt;, Wells Fargo is &lt;code&gt;wf.wd1/WellsFargoJobs&lt;/code&gt;. Many companies also run several sites: one for experienced hires, one for students, one per country.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


2. List the jobs
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The API lives on the same host, under &lt;code&gt;/wday/cxs/{tenant}/{site}&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;curl -s https://nvidia.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/nvidia/NVIDIAExternalCareerSite/jobs \
-H &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Content-Type: application/json'&lt;/span&gt; \
-d &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'{"appliedFacets":{},"limit":20,"offset":0,"searchText":"security"}'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The answer looks like this (shortened):&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"total"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;413&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"jobPostings"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"title"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Director, Global Event Security"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"externalPath"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/job/US-CA-Santa-Clara/Director--Global-Event-Security_JR2023116"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"locationsText"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"US, CA, Santa Clara"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"postedOn"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Posted 30+ Days Ago"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"bulletFields"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"JR2023116"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"facets"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="err"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;searchText&lt;/code&gt; is Workday's own keyword search. Leave it empty to get everything. Page through with &lt;code&gt;offset&lt;/code&gt; in steps of 20.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


3. The four gotchas
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pages hold at most 20 jobs.&lt;/strong&gt; Ask for &lt;code&gt;"limit": 50&lt;/code&gt; and you get HTTP 400. Twenty is the maximum.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;total&lt;/code&gt; often comes only with the first page.&lt;/strong&gt; On many sites later pages report &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt;, so read it from &lt;code&gt;offset: 0&lt;/code&gt; and keep it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Many sites return at most 2,000 jobs per search, and they do not tell you.&lt;/strong&gt; Past offset 2,000 they quietly send the first page again. A loop that stops on an empty page will never stop, and a loop that counts pages will collect the same 20 jobs over and over. These sites also report &lt;code&gt;total: 2000&lt;/code&gt; when they have more: NVIDIA reports 2,000 and has 2,692. Other sites have no such limit. CVS Health reports its real total, about 18,000, and pages through all of it. One request at offset 2,000 tells you which kind you have: if it repeats the first page, the site is capped.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dates are relative.&lt;/strong&gt; The list says "Posted Today" or "Posted 30+ Days Ago". The exact date is only in the job details (next section).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Getting past 2,000 on capped sites
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The answer also carries &lt;code&gt;facets&lt;/code&gt;: the site's own filters with a job count for each value, such as job family, worker type, time type and location. Pick a facet where every value has fewer than 2,000 jobs, run one search per value, and merge the results by &lt;code&gt;externalPath&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"appliedFacets"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"jobFamilyGroup"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&amp;lt;id from facets&amp;gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"limit"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;20&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"offset"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"searchText"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;On very large capped sites one facet is not enough, because even the biggest slice is over 2,000. Then you nest filters: split that slice again by location or worker type.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


4. Job details
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Each job's &lt;code&gt;externalPath&lt;/code&gt; gives you the full posting:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;curl -s https://nvidia.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/wday/cxs/nvidia/NVIDIAExternalCareerSite/job/US-CA-Santa-Clara/Director--Global-Event-Security_JR2023116
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Look inside &lt;code&gt;jobPostingInfo&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Field&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What it is&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;jobDescription&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Full description as HTML&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;startDate&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Exact posting date&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;location&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;additionalLocations&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Every location of the job, not just "2 Locations"&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;timeType&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Full time or part time&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;remoteType&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Remote, hybrid or on-site, when the company sets it&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;jobReqId&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Requisition ID&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;externalUrl&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Link candidates use to apply&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There is no salary field. US employers publish pay ranges inside the description, in formats like &lt;code&gt;$100,000.00 - $179,000.00&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;232,000 USD – 368,000 USD&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;USD 120,000 - 150,000&lt;/code&gt;, so you parse them from the text.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


5. The whole thing in one script
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;About 90 lines of Python, standard library only. It reads the site from a URL, pages through the search, checks whether the site is capped, splits capped sites by one facet, and prints the first few jobs with details:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;python workday_jobs_example.py https://nvidia.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/NVIDIAExternalCareerSite
&lt;span class="c"&gt;# 2692 jobs&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c"&gt;# Senior QA Engineer, System Product Engineering | Israel, Yokneam | 2026-11-15 | https://nvidia.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The script is on GitHub: &lt;a href="https://github.com/johnkaa/workday-jobs-api" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;github.com/johnkaa/workday-jobs-api&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


6. Where to find Workday sites
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There is no public list of companies that use Workday. You can build one from the &lt;a href="https://index.commoncrawl.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Common Crawl URL index&lt;/a&gt;: search it for &lt;code&gt;*.myworkdayjobs.com&lt;/code&gt;, collect the tenant and site pairs, and check each one with a single &lt;code&gt;/jobs&lt;/code&gt; request. That is how I put together a list of more than 3,000 live career sites. The 500 biggest are in the same repository.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Be a good guest
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is public data that companies publish for anyone to read, but it is still somebody's server. Keep a few requests in flight at most, cache what you can, and do not fetch descriptions you do not need.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


If you would rather not maintain this
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I packaged all of the above as &lt;a href="https://apify.com/makerio/workday-jobs" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Workday Jobs Scraper&lt;/a&gt; on Apify. You paste a career site URL or type a company name, or you search one keyword across all 3,000+ sites at once. It handles both kinds of big sites: NVIDIA returns all 2,692 jobs through nested filters, CVS Health all 18,047 by paging straight through. It also parses salaries, filters by location, remote type and posting date, and can return only jobs that are new since the last run. It costs $1.00 per 1,000 jobs. Apify's free plan includes $5 of usage every month, enough for about 5,000 jobs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you also need Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby, SmartRecruiters and other job boards in the same format, &lt;a href="https://apify.com/makerio/career-site-jobs" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Career Site Jobs Scraper&lt;/a&gt; covers nine of them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


Automating Bluesky JSON Payload Generation for Content‑Automation
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TL;DR:&lt;/strong&gt; I fixed the bug that prevented the automatic creation of the Bluesky JSON payload and wired it into our daily content‑automation pipeline. The fix updates the payload schema, adds proper date handling, and syncs the metadata flags so the next publish runs without manual intervention.  &lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


The Problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our content‑automation repo publishes the same article to Medium, Substack, and Bluesky every day. While the Medium and Substack pipelines were working, the Bluesky step kept failing with the following error in the CI logs:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Error: JSON validation failed – property "date" is required
at validatePayload (/usr/src/app/publish/bluesky.js:45:13)
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;bluesky_es.json&lt;/code&gt; file was either missing or contained an incomplete payload, causing the &lt;code&gt;publish/bluesky.js&lt;/code&gt; script to abort. The symptom was a &lt;code&gt;bluesky_published: false&lt;/code&gt; flag left untouched in &lt;code&gt;metadata.json&lt;/code&gt;, which meant the article never appeared on Bluesky.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What I Tried First
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My first attempt was to patch the missing fields directly in the generated JSON after the script ran:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// quick‑and‑dirty fix (did not commit)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;parse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;fs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;readFileSync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'bluesky_es.json'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;date&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toISOString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;fs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;writeFileSync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'bluesky_es.json'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;I added this snippet at the end of &lt;code&gt;publish/bluesky.js&lt;/code&gt; and re‑ran the workflow. The script no longer threw a validation error, but the JSON file still lacked the required &lt;code&gt;type&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;text&lt;/code&gt; fields for some articles, resulting in a partially published post. Moreover, the hack was brittle: any future schema change would break it again.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The Implementation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


1. Refactor the payload builder
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The core issue was that &lt;code&gt;generateBlueskyPayload()&lt;/code&gt; assumed every article had a &lt;code&gt;summary&lt;/code&gt; field, which is optional in our markdown front‑matter. When &lt;code&gt;summary&lt;/code&gt; was missing, the function returned &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; for the &lt;code&gt;text&lt;/code&gt; property, causing the validation error.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/publish/bluesky.js&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;generateBlueskyPayload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;mdMeta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mdMeta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;summary&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mdMeta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;summary&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mdMeta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;excerpt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'No summary available'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'avance'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;               &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// &amp;lt;-- hard‑coded to match our content type&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toISOString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;language&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mdMeta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;lang&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'es'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;I added a fallback to &lt;code&gt;mdMeta.excerpt&lt;/code&gt; and finally a default string, guaranteeing that &lt;code&gt;text&lt;/code&gt; is never undefined.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


2. Update the JSON schema validator
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The validator previously required &lt;code&gt;date&lt;/code&gt; but not &lt;code&gt;language&lt;/code&gt;. I extended it to enforce &lt;code&gt;type&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;text&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;language&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/publish/validateBluesky.js&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;schema&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'object'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;required&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'type'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'text'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'date'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'language'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;properties&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'string'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;enum&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'avance'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'nota'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'string'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;minLength&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'string'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;format&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'date-time'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;language&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'string'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;enum&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'es'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'en'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now the script fails fast with a clear message if any required field is missing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


3. Wire the generator into the daily run
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The daily pipeline lives in &lt;code&gt;.github/workflows/content.yml&lt;/code&gt;. I added a new step that runs the Bluesky generator after the Medium and Substack steps:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight yaml"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# .github/workflows/content.yml
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;Generate Bluesky payload&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s"&gt;node src/publish/bluesky.js \&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s"&gt;--input content/$(date +%Y/%m/%d)/content-automation/metadata.json \&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s"&gt;--output content/$(date +%Y/%m/%d)/content-automation/bluesky_es.json&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;Commit Bluesky JSON&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;uses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;stefanzweifel/git-auto-commit-action@v4&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;commit_message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"chore(bluesky): posts $(date +%Y-%m-%d) [skip ci]"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;file_pattern&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"content/**/bluesky_es.json"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This step guarantees the payload is generated &lt;strong&gt;before&lt;/strong&gt; we attempt to publish.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


4. Sync metadata flags
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;metadata.json&lt;/code&gt; tracks which channels have been generated. The previous commit only toggled &lt;code&gt;bluesky_published&lt;/code&gt; after a successful post, leaving the generation flag out of sync. I added a &lt;code&gt;bluesky_generated&lt;/code&gt; boolean that flips to &lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt; right after the JSON file is written:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/publish/bluesky.js (excerpt)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;fs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;writeFileSync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;outputPath&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;updateMetadata&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;bluesky_generated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;And the metadata schema now looks like:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"medium_generated"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"substack_generated"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"bluesky_generated"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"bluesky_published"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"bluesky_uris"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


5. Verify with a diff of the changed files
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Below are the relevant diffs that landed in the three commits:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+// src/publish/bluesky.js (new fallback logic)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+function generateBlueskyPayload(mdMeta) {&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  const text = mdMeta.summary&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+    ? mdMeta.summary&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+    : mdMeta.excerpt || 'No summary available';&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  return {&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+    type: 'avance',&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+    text,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+    date: new Date().toISOString(),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+    language: mdMeta.lang || 'es',&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  };&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+// src/publish/validateBluesky.js (extended schema)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+required: ['type', 'text', 'date', 'language'],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+// .github/workflows/content.yml (new step)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+- name: Generate Bluesky payload&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  run: |&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+    node src/publish/bluesky.js \&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+      --input content/$(date +%Y/%m/%d)/content-automation/metadata.json \&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+      --output content/$(date +%Y/%m/%d)/content-automation/bluesky_es.json&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+// content/2026/11/13/content-automation/bluesky_es.json (generated)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  {&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+    "type": "avance",&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+    "text": "Finalmente resolví el bug que bloqueaba la generación automática del JSON para Bluesky. Ahora el archivo bluesky_es.json incluye los tres ...",&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+    "date": "2026-11-14T08:12:00.000Z",&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+    "language": "es"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  }&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+// content/2026/11/13/content-automation/metadata.json (updated flags)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  "medium_generated": true,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  "substack_generated": true,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  "bluesky_generated": true,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  "bluesky_published": false,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  "bluesky_uris": {}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


Key Takeaway
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Never assume optional front‑matter fields exist when building payloads for external APIs. Always provide deterministic fallbacks and validate the full schema &lt;strong&gt;before&lt;/strong&gt; you hand the payload to the publishing client. This prevents silent data loss and makes CI failures easier to diagnose.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What's Next
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add unit tests for `generateBlues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Part of my &lt;a href="https://dev.to/zaerohell"&gt;Build in Public&lt;/a&gt; series — sharing the real process of building SaaS projects from Playa del Carmen, México.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Repo: &lt;code&gt;zaerohell/content-automation&lt;/code&gt; · 2026-11-14&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;#playadev #buildinpublic&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Synchronous HTTP code is simple.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But sometimes your application needs to call several APIs at once, reduce waiting time, or avoid tying up threads while requests are in flight.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That is where asynchronous programming becomes useful.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In this tutorial, we'll build on Java's built-in &lt;code&gt;HttpClient&lt;/code&gt; and explore:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;sendAsync()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Running multiple HTTP requests concurrently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Combining several API responses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handling async errors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Applying timeouts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using Jackson with asynchronous responses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comparing &lt;code&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/code&gt; with virtual threads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding when async code is actually worth using&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;By the end, you'll have several practical patterns for building concurrent REST clients in modern Java.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


1. Synchronous vs Asynchronous HTTP
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A normal synchronous request looks like this:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;send&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;BodyHandlers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;ofString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The current thread waits until the response arrives.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Conceptually:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Send request
↓
Wait
↓
Wait
↓
Receive response
↓
Continue
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This is easy to understand.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But if you need to call three independent APIs:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;API A → 2 seconds
API B → 3 seconds
API C → 1 second
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;and you call them one after another, the total time can be roughly:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;2 + 3 + 1 = 6 seconds
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That is where concurrency can help.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


2. &lt;code&gt;HttpClient.sendAsync()&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Java's &lt;code&gt;HttpClient&lt;/code&gt; has an asynchronous method:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sendAsync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Instead of returning:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;it returns:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;future&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sendAsync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;BodyHandlers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;ofString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The request starts, but the current thread does not block waiting for the result.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


3. Your First Async Request
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let's create a simple example.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;java&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;net&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;URI&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;java&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;net&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;http&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;java&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;net&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;http&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpRequest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;java&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;net&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;http&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;java&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;util&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;concurrent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;AsyncExample&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;static&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;args&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpClient&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;newHttpClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpRequest&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpRequest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;newBuilder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;uri&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;URI&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;create&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts/1"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;GET&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;future&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sendAsync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;BodyHandlers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;ofString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;future&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;thenAccept&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;System&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;out&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;println&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;statusCode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;System&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;out&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;println&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;future&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The important line is:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;future&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;thenAccept&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This says:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When the response arrives, run this code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


4. What Does &lt;code&gt;join()&lt;/code&gt; Do?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In the previous example, we used:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;future&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Why?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Because this is a small console application.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Without it, the main method could finish before the asynchronous response is processed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;join()&lt;/code&gt; waits for the &lt;code&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/code&gt; to complete.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So although the HTTP operation is asynchronous, our demo waits at the end so the application stays alive.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In larger applications, you often won't call &lt;code&gt;join()&lt;/code&gt; immediately.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


5. &lt;code&gt;thenApply()&lt;/code&gt; vs &lt;code&gt;thenAccept()&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These two methods are commonly used with &lt;code&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


&lt;code&gt;thenAccept()&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use it when you want to consume a result but not return another value.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;future&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;thenAccept&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;System&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;out&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;println&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


&lt;code&gt;thenApply()&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use it when you want to transform the result.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;bodyFuture&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;future&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;thenApply&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;bodyFuture&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;is:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;rather than:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


6. Transforming an HTTP Response
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A common pattern is:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sendAsync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;BodyHandlers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;ofString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;thenApply&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This is much cleaner if you only care about the body.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But in production code, you should usually check the status code first.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


7. Validate the Status Code
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let's create a helper:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;static&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;validate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kt"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;statusCode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;200&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;RuntimeException&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"HTTP "&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;": "&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;bodyFuture&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sendAsync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;BodyHandlers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;ofString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;thenApply&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;AsyncExample&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;validate&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;thenApply&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The flow becomes:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;sendAsync()
↓
validate()
↓
extract body
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


8. Add Jackson
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Now let's combine async HTTP with Jackson.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Suppose an API returns:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"id"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"title"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Hello"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"body"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Example"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"userId"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Create a record:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;record&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kt"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kt"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kt"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kt"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then use Jackson:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ObjectMapper&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mapper&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ObjectMapper&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;We can parse the response asynchronously.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


9. Async JSON Deserialization
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;postFuture&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sendAsync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;BodyHandlers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;ofString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;thenApply&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;AsyncExample&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;validate&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;thenApply&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;thenApply&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mapper&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;readValue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Exception&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;RuntimeException&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;postFuture&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;is:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Usage:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Post&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;post&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;postFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;System&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;out&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;println&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


10. Create a Reusable Async GET Method
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let's make the pattern reusable.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;getAsync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kt"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Class&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;responseType&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpRequest&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpRequest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;newBuilder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;uri&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;URI&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;create&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;header&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Accept"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"application/json"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;GET&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sendAsync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;BodyHandlers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;ofString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;thenApply&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;validate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;thenApply&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mapper&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;readValue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;responseType&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;IOException&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletionException&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now calling an API becomes:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;User&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;future&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;restClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getAsync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"https://example.com/users/1"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;User&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


11. Why &lt;code&gt;CompletionException&lt;/code&gt;?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Inside a &lt;code&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/code&gt; pipeline, checked exceptions are awkward.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Jackson can throw:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;IOException&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;but a lambda passed to &lt;code&gt;thenApply()&lt;/code&gt; cannot simply throw it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A common pattern is:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletionException&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This wraps the checked exception inside an unchecked exception that works naturally with &lt;code&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


12. Run Multiple Requests Concurrently
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is where async becomes especially useful.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Suppose we want:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;/users/1
/posts/1
/todos/1
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;We can start all three requests immediately:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;User&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;userFuture&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getAsync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;userUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;User&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;postFuture&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getAsync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;postUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Todo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;todoFuture&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getAsync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;todoUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Todo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;At this point, all three requests can be in flight at the same time.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


13. Sequential vs Concurrent Timing
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sequential:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Request A
↓
wait
↓
Request B
↓
wait
↓
Request C
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Concurrent:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Request A ──────────────┐
Request B ──────────┐   │
Request C ───────┐  │   │
↓  ↓   ↓
results arrive
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;If the requests are independent, concurrent execution can reduce total waiting time significantly.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


14. Combine Two Futures with &lt;code&gt;thenCombine()&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Suppose we want to combine:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;User&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;and:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;List&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;We can use:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;thenCombine&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;UserProfile&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;profileFuture&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;userFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;thenCombine&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;postsFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;posts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;UserProfile&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;posts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;profileFuture&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;contains both results.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


15. Example &lt;code&gt;UserProfile&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;record&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;UserProfile&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;User&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kt"&gt;List&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;posts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;UserProfile&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;profile&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;profileFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This is useful when several endpoints contribute to one final result.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


16. Combine Many Futures with &lt;code&gt;allOf()&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;thenCombine()&lt;/code&gt; works well for two futures.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For many futures, use:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;allOf&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;User&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;userFuture&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getUser&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;List&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;postsFuture&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getPosts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;List&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Todo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;todosFuture&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getTodos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;Void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;all&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;allOf&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;userFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;postsFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;todosFuture&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Wait for all:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;all&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then retrieve:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;User&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;userFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kt"&gt;List&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;posts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;postsFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kt"&gt;List&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Todo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;todos&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;todosFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


17. Build the Final Object After &lt;code&gt;allOf()&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A cleaner approach:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dashboard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dashboardFuture&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;allOf&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;userFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;postsFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;todosFuture&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;thenApply&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ignored&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dashboard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;userFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;postsFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;todosFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dashboard&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dashboard&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;dashboardFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


18. A Helper for Lists of Futures
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Suppose we have:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;List&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;User&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;and want:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;List&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;User&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;We can create:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;static&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;List&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;sequence&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kt"&gt;List&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;futures&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;Void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;all&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;allOf&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;futures&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toArray&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;all&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;thenApply&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;ignored&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;futures&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stream&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toList&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Usage:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;List&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;User&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;futures&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;ids&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stream&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getAsync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/users/"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;User&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toList&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;List&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;User&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;usersFuture&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sequence&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;futures&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This is a very useful pattern.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


19. But Don't Launch Unlimited Requests
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There is an important danger.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;000&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;IDs&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;and you do:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ids&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stream&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;getAsync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toList&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;You might launch thousands of HTTP requests at once.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That can:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overload the remote API&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hit rate limits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exhaust resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create huge memory pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Concurrency still needs limits.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


20. Limit Concurrency
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One simple approach is batching.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead of:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;10,000 concurrent requests
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;do:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;50 at a time
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;batchSize&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;50&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then process IDs in batches.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Conceptually:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Batch 1
→ 50 requests
→ wait

Batch 2
→ 50 requests
→ wait

Batch 3
→ 50 requests
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This is often safer than unlimited concurrency.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


21. Async Error Handling with &lt;code&gt;exceptionally()&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Suppose a request fails.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can handle it using:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;exceptionally&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;User&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;future&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getAsync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;User&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;exceptionally&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;System&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;println&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This converts the failed future into a successful future containing:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That can be useful, but be careful.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Returning &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; can hide failures.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


22. Use &lt;code&gt;handle()&lt;/code&gt; When You Need Both Cases
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;handle()&lt;/code&gt; receives both:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;result
error
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;future&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;handle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;System&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;println&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Request failed: "&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fallbackUser&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This is useful for fallback logic.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


23. Use &lt;code&gt;whenComplete()&lt;/code&gt; for Logging
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sometimes you don't want to change the result.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You just want to observe it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;whenComplete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;future&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;whenComplete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;System&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;println&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Failed: "&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;else&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;System&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;out&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;println&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Request completed"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The original future result continues unchanged.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


24. &lt;code&gt;exceptionally()&lt;/code&gt; vs &lt;code&gt;handle()&lt;/code&gt; vs &lt;code&gt;whenComplete()&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A useful rule:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;exceptionally()
→ recover only from failure

handle()
→ transform success or failure

whenComplete()
→ observe success or failure
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


25. Add Async Timeouts
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/code&gt; provides timeout helpers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Fail after a timeout
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;future&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;orTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="mi"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;TimeUnit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;SECONDS&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;If the future does not complete in time, it fails.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Return a fallback value
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;future&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;completeOnTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;fallbackUser&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="mi"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;TimeUnit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;SECONDS&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This can be useful in applications where partial results are acceptable.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


26. HTTP Timeout vs Future Timeout
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These are different.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


&lt;code&gt;HttpRequest.timeout(...)&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Controls the HTTP request.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpRequest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;newBuilder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;timeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Duration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;ofSeconds&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


&lt;code&gt;CompletableFuture.orTimeout(...)&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Controls the future pipeline.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;future&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;orTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="mi"&gt;12&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;TimeUnit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;SECONDS&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Using both can provide stronger protection.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


27. Async POST Requests
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;POST can also be asynchronous.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;R&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;R&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;postAsync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kt"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;requestBody&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Class&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;R&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;responseType&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kt"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;mapper&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;writeValueAsString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;requestBody&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpRequest&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpRequest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;newBuilder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;uri&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;URI&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;create&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;header&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Content-Type"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"application/json"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;POST&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpRequest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;BodyPublishers&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;ofString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sendAsync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;BodyHandlers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;ofString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;thenApply&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;validate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;thenApply&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mapper&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;readValue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;responseType&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;IOException&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletionException&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;IOException&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;failedFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


28. Why &lt;code&gt;failedFuture()&lt;/code&gt; Is Useful
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Suppose serialization fails before the HTTP request starts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We still want to return:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;R&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;instead of throwing immediately.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Java provides:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;failedFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;So the caller sees the failure through the same async API.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


29. Build an Async &lt;code&gt;RestClient&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let's create a more complete version.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;fasterxml&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;jackson&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;databind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DeserializationFeature&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;fasterxml&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;jackson&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;databind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ObjectMapper&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;java&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;io&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;IOException&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;java&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;net&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;URI&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;java&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;net&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;http&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;java&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;net&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;http&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpRequest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;java&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;net&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;http&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;java&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Duration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;java&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;util&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;concurrent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletableFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;java&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;util&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;concurrent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CompletionException&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;AsyncRestClient&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;final&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;HttpClient&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;final&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ObjectMapper&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mapper&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

